@page "/visitorinfo"
<PageTitle>Taniti : Visitor Info</PageTitle>

<div class="card mb-4 visitor-card">
    <div class="card-header custom-header">
        Visitor Information
    </div>
    <div class="card-body text-center">
        <p class="card-text">
            Essential travel details to help you prepare for your visit to Taniti.
        </p>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-group list-group-flush text-start">
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Power outlets are 120 volts (same as the United States).
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Alcohol cannot be sold or served between midnight and 9:00 a.m.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            The drinking age is 18, and enforcement is not strict.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Many younger Tanitians speak fluent English; rural areas have less English fluency.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            One hospital and several clinics are available, with multilingual staff.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Violent crime is rare, but pickpocketing and petty theft have increased with tourism.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Taniti observes many national holidays; attractions and restaurants may close.
        </li>
        <li class="list-group-item">
            Currency: U.S. dollars are standard; euros and yen are often accepted. Banks offer exchange services.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="flex flex-row d-flex">
        <img src="images/beaches02.jpg" alt="Island Image" class="visitor-image card-img-bottom"/>
        <img src="images/tourists.jpg" alt="Island Image" class="visitor-image card-img-bottom"/>
        <img src="images/beaches03.jpg" alt="Island Image" class="visitor-image card-img-bottom"/>      
    </div>

</div>